# Phase 2 CLI acceptance — normalization introspection (M1c, P2-T23/T24).

`QAI_DATA_DIR` points the real `qai` binary at a fresh temp database (set by the
harness). The normalize commands prove the migration seed on every call: profile
definitions come from seeded rows, implementations from code.

```console
$ qai db migrate
migrations applied; schema version [..]

```

```console
$ qai quran normalize --list-profiles
L0.exact@1.0.0 — Exact canonical [indexed]
L1.ws@1.0.0 — Exact after whitespace normalization [indexed]
L2.marks@1.0.0 — Ignore Quranic marks [indexed]
L3.diacritics@1.0.0 — Ignore diacritics [indexed]
L4.hamza@1.0.0 — Normalize hamza/alif [indexed]
L5.codepoints@1.0.0 — Normalize Arabic/Persian code points [indexed]
L6.skeleton@1.0.0 — Space-insensitive skeleton [indexed]
L7.affix@1.0.0 — Morphological (heuristic affix) search [indexed, heuristic]
L8.fuzzy@1.0.0 — Fuzzy spelling search [query-time, experimental]

```

```console
$ qai quran normalize --show-rule N06
N06 normalize_hamza_forms [deterministic] v1.0.0
Fold hamza carriers to bare alef/waw/yeh; standalone hamza deleted

```

```console
$ qai quran normalize "بِسْمِ" --profile L3.diacritics
input: بِسْمِ
output: بسم
profile: L3.diacritics@1.0.0

```

`--explain` prints the rule-by-rule transformation with the trace label.

```console
$ qai quran normalize "بِسْمِ" --profile L3.diacritics --explain
input: بِسْمِ
profile: L3.diacritics@1.0.0
output: بسم
rules applied (8):
  N01 whitespace_collapse [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بِسْمِ
  N11 strip_zero_width_and_bidi [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بِسْمِ
  N16 nfc [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بِسْمِ
  N04 strip_quranic_marks [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بِسْمِ
  N14 strip_pause_marks [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بِسْمِ
  N03 strip_harakat [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بسم
  N05 strip_superscript_alef [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بسم
  N02 strip_tatweel [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → بسم

```

Heuristic profiles carry the mandatory label.

```console
$ qai quran normalize "والكتب" --profile L7.affix --explain
input: والكتب
profile: L7.affix@1.0.0
output: الكتب
rules applied (19):
  N01 whitespace_collapse [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N11 strip_zero_width_and_bidi [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N16 nfc [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N04 strip_quranic_marks [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N14 strip_pause_marks [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N03 strip_harakat [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N05 strip_superscript_alef [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N02 strip_tatweel [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N07 normalize_wasla [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N06 normalize_hamza_forms [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N08 normalize_alif_maqsura [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N10 normalize_persian_codepoints [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N13 fold_digits [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N09 normalize_ta_marbuta [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N15 expand_presentation_forms [deterministic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N18 strip_definite_article [heuristic] v1.0.0
    → والكتب
  N19 strip_conjunction_prefix [heuristic] v1.0.0
    → الكتب
  N20 strip_preposition_prefix [heuristic] v1.0.0
    → الكتب
  N21 strip_pronoun_suffix [heuristic] v1.0.0
    → الكتب
note: matched using heuristic affix stripping — not verified scholarship

```

Adhoc rule lists work without a profile, and `--profile` with `--rules` is a
usage error.

```console
$ qai quran normalize "بِسْمِ" --rules N01,N03
input: بِسْمِ
output: بسم
profile: adhoc:bdfecf81301d

```

```console
$ qai quran normalize "x" --profile L3.diacritics --rules N01
? 2
error: use either --profile or --rules, never both

```

Unknown profiles and rules fail with actionable errors.

```console
$ qai quran normalize "x" --profile L9.nope
? 2
error: unknown normalization profile 'L9.nope'

```

```console
$ qai quran normalize --show-rule N23
N23 transliterate is reserved for Phase 4 (transliteration/phonetics)

```

Derived forms rebuild against a real edition (MV-018 verified before and
after; canonical text untouched).

```console
$ qai quran import ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-min/manifest.json
imported test-edition-min@0.1.0 to Staged

```

```console
$ qai quran activate test-edition-min@0.1.0 --yes
activated test-edition-min@0.1.0 (generation 1)

```

```console
$ qai quran forms rebuild test-edition-min@0.1.0
rebuilt forms for quran-edition:test-edition-min@0.1.0: 14 ayahs, 64 tokens, 18 skeletons (generation 1)
MV-018 canonical-unchanged: pass (sha256:235795cb218c2df44496265b4ba5c3377d48944cb28cc4ff64c6104770932704)
provenance: prov-forms-test-edition-min-0.1.0-g1-75e0e98f12bf

```

```console
$ qai quran forms rebuild bad-ref
? 2
error: use slug@version

```

Index builds stage a fresh generation, verify it, and flip the pointer
atomically; the previous generation stays on disk.

```console
$ qai quran index rebuild
index quran.ayah.v1 generation 1 active: 14 docs (corpus generation 1)
manifest: sha256:9d1c3cfec9084d2471310ae8319fa06ec2a216decdf66dfe4eee6127dd056c2c
previous generation: none

```

```console
$ qai quran index verify
index quran.ayah.v1 generation 1 healthy: 14 docs

```

```console
$ qai quran index rebuild
index quran.ayah.v1 generation 2 active: 14 docs (corpus generation 1)
manifest: sha256:9d1c3cfec9084d2471310ae8319fa06ec2a216decdf66dfe4eee6127dd056c2c
previous generation: 1

```
